stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> WATCHING: risk admitted with an observable trigger, a named watcher and a cadence

    WATCHING --> WATCHING: cadence review finds no trigger, watch date stamped
    WATCHING --> TRIGGERED: the named observable is observed by the named watcher
    WATCHING --> UNOBSERVABLE: the cadence review cannot name where the trigger would be seen
    UNOBSERVABLE --> WATCHING: trigger rewritten as something a specific person can watch for

    TRIGGERED --> RESPONDING: the pre-agreed response fires, owner logs the start time
    TRIGGERED --> FALSE_POSITIVE: the observable is confirmed not to be the trigger
    FALSE_POSITIVE --> WATCHING: trigger wording tightened so it does not fire the same way twice

    RESPONDING --> MITIGATED: the response completes and the residual is re-stated
    RESPONDING --> ESCALATED: the response does not hold or the owner cannot act alone
    ESCALATED --> MITIGATED: escalated decision taken and logged
    ESCALATED --> THESIS_REVIEW: the risk is named in a whole thesis kill condition

    MITIGATED --> WATCHING: the trigger can recur
    MITIGATED --> RETIRED: the validation that retires this risk closed PASS
    WATCHING --> RETIRED: the condition that created the risk no longer exists

    RETIRED --> WATCHING: a later capture shows the condition has returned

    note right of TRIGGERED
        The moment of the trigger is never
        the moment of the argument.
        The response was agreed in advance.
    end note

    note right of UNOBSERVABLE
        A risk with no observable trigger
        is an anxiety, not a register row.
    end note
